# Authorization server: metadata and token exchange (LWS 1.0 core sections 5.2.2-5.2.3).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: "LWS 1.0 core: authorization server"
comment: >-
  Tests of the storage's authorization server, which the harness finds the way a client
  does: an anonymous request to the test container yields a challenge whose as_uri is the
  authorization server, whose metadata sits at the RFC 8414 well-known location for
  lws-configuration, and whose token endpoint performs RFC 8693 token exchange. A
  did:key credential is the vehicle wherever a valid subject token is needed, because it
  needs no trust set up in advance; those tests apply only when the metadata lists did:key
  among its subject identifier types.
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/
entries:

  - id: "#authz-server-metadata-well-known"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: authz-server-metadata-well-known
    label: The authorization server publishes RFC 8414 metadata at lws-configuration
    comment: >-
      Discovered from the challenge rather than a host name assumed in advance. The
      issuer must be the identifier the well-known URL was built from (RFC 8414 section
      3.3), the token endpoint and jwks_uri must be named, and token exchange must be
      among the grant types, since the RFC 8414 default excludes it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-server-metadata
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-exchange-request
      - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8414#section-3
    traits: [Get, Discovery, Authz, TokenExchange]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-server-metadata-well-known
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-exchange-grant
    mirrors: lws10/manifest.jsonld#authz-server-metadata-well-known
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "${as.metadataUrl}"
      accept: application/json
    response:
      statusCode: 200
      contentType: application/json
      json:
        - pointer: /issuer
          equals: "${as.uri}"
        - pointer: /token_endpoint
          jsonType: string
        - pointer: /jwks_uri
          jsonType: string
        - pointer: /grant_types_supported
          hasValue: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange

  - id: "#authz-metadata-subject-token-types"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: authz-metadata-subject-token-types
    label: The metadata advertises the subject token types it accepts
    comment: >-
      "An authorization server SHOULD advertise the subject tokens that it supports."
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-server-metadata
    traits: [Get, Discovery, TokenExchange]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-metadata-subject-token-types
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "${as.metadataUrl}"
      accept: application/json
    response:
      statusCode: 200
      json:
        - pointer: /subject_token_types_supported
          jsonType: array

  - id: "#authz-metadata-subject-identifier-types"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: authz-metadata-subject-identifier-types
    label: The metadata advertises the subject identifier types it accepts
    comment: >-
      New in the 21 September 2026 draft; SHOULD be advertised, and defaults to ["https"]
      when omitted.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-server-metadata
    traits: [Get, Discovery, TokenExchange]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    note: Uncatalogued; the clause is newer than the catalog baseline.
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "${as.metadataUrl}"
      accept: application/json
    response:
      statusCode: 200
      json:
        - pointer: /subject_identifier_types_supported
          jsonType: array

  - id: "#authz-token-exchange-valid"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: authz-token-exchange-valid
    label: Token exchange issues an RFC 9068 access token for the storage
    comment: >-
      The response must follow RFC 6749 section 5.1 and RFC 8693 (issued_token_type is
      REQUIRED, Cache-Control no-store is a MUST), and the access token must be an RFC 9068
      JWT, verifiable against the published keys, carrying iss, aud naming the storage,
      sub naming the agent, client_id, exp, iat and jti. lws-test-suite compared the whole
      response to a fixture holding a placeholder token and no issued_token_type.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-exchange-request
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-exchange-response
      - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749#section-5.1
      - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693#section-2.2.1
      - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9068#section-2
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange, Authn]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-exchange-grant
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-exchange-resource-param
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-exchange-subject-token-param
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-validate-before-issuing
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-response-rfc6749-rfc9068
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-access-token-iss-claim
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-access-token-aud-claim
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-access-token-sub-claim
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-access-token-client-id-claim
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-access-token-exp-short-lived
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-access-token-iat-claim
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-access-token-jti-claim
    mirrors: lws10/manifest.jsonld#authz-token-exchange-valid
    steps:
      - label: the authorization server accepts did:key subjects (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${as.metadataUrl}"
          accept: application/json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /subject_identifier_types_supported
              hasValue: did:key
            - pointer: /subject_token_types_supported
              optional: true
              hasValue: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
      - label: exchange a did:key credential for an access token to the storage
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${as.tokenEndpoint}"
          bodyForm:
            grant_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
            resource: "${as.realm}"
            subject_token: "${credential.didkey}"
            subject_token_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/json
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Cache-Control
              matches: '(?i)\bno-store\b'
          json:
            - pointer: /access_token
              jsonType: string
              capture: accessToken
            - pointer: /token_type
              matches: '(?i)^bearer$'
            - pointer: /issued_token_type
              jsonType: string
          jwt:
            token: "${accessToken}"
            jwks: "${as.jwksUri}"
            header:
              - pointer: /typ
                matches: '(?i)^(application/)?at\+jwt$'
            claims:
              - pointer: /iss
                equals: "${as.issuer}"
              - pointer: /aud
                hasValue: "${as.realm}"
              - pointer: /sub
                equals: "${identity.didkey.webid}"
              - pointer: /client_id
                jsonType: string
              - pointer: /exp
                jsonType: number
              - pointer: /iat
                jsonType: number
              - pointer: /jti
                jsonType: string

  - id: "#authz-token-exchange-invalid-resource"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: authz-token-exchange-invalid-resource
    label: Token exchange for an unknown storage is refused with an OAuth error
    comment: >-
      "The authorization server MUST reject any request in which the resource parameter
      identifies an unknown or untrusted storage." RFC 8693 section 2.2.2 says
      invalid_target SHOULD be used for exactly this; the draft's example shows
      invalid_request. Either is accepted.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-exchange-request
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-exchange-response
      - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693#section-2.2.2
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-exchange-resource-param
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-error-rfc6749
    mirrors: lws10/manifest.jsonld#authz-token-exchange-invalid-resource
    steps:
      - label: the authorization server accepts did:key subjects (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${as.metadataUrl}"
          accept: application/json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /subject_identifier_types_supported
              hasValue: did:key
      - label: ask for a token to a storage the server has never heard of
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${as.tokenEndpoint}"
          bodyForm:
            grant_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
            resource: https://unknown-storage.invalid/
            subject_token: "${credential.didkey}"
            subject_token_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
        response:
          statusCode: 400
          contentType: application/json
          json:
            - pointer: /error
              matches: '^(invalid_target|invalid_request)$'

  - id: "#authz-token-exchange-missing-resource"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: authz-token-exchange-missing-resource
    label: Token exchange without a resource parameter is refused with invalid_request
    comment: >-
      The resource parameter is REQUIRED; RFC 6749 names invalid_request for a missing
      required parameter.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-exchange-request
      - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749#section-5.2
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-exchange-resource-param
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-error-rfc6749
    steps:
      - label: the authorization server accepts did:key subjects (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${as.metadataUrl}"
          accept: application/json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /subject_identifier_types_supported
              hasValue: did:key
      - label: exchange a valid credential without naming a resource
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${as.tokenEndpoint}"
          bodyForm:
            grant_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
            subject_token: "${credential.didkey}"
            subject_token_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
        response:
          statusCode: 400
          contentType: application/json
          json:
            - pointer: /error
              equals: invalid_request

  - id: "#authz-token-exchange-missing-subject-token"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: authz-token-exchange-missing-subject-token
    label: Token exchange without a subject token is refused with invalid_request
    comment: >-
      The subject_token parameter is REQUIRED. Suite-independent, so it lives here
      rather than in the did:key manifest where lws-test-suite put it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-exchange-request
      - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749#section-5.2
    traits: [Post, TokenExchange]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-exchange-subject-token-param
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-error-rfc6749
    mirrors: lws10/auth/did_key/manifest.jsonld#authn-didkey-missing-credential
    request:
      method: POST
      url: "${as.tokenEndpoint}"
      bodyForm:
        grant_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
        resource: "${as.realm}"
        subject_token_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
    response:
      statusCode: 400
      contentType: application/json
      json:
        - pointer: /error
          equals: invalid_request

  - id: "#authz-issued-token-accepted-by-storage"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: authz-issued-token-accepted-by-storage
    label: The storage accepts an access token its authorization server issued
    comment: >-
      Closes the loop between the two servers: a token fresh from the storage's own
      authorization server must pass the storage's validation. The did:key agent owns
      nothing, so the storage may still deny access (403, or 404 to hide existence);
      what it must not do is answer 401, which would call a valid token invalid.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-validation-verification
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#authorization-token-exchange-response
    traits: [Post, Get, TokenExchange, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    as: anonymous
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-token-validation-checklist
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-jwt-signature-jwks-rotation
    steps:
      - label: the authorization server accepts did:key subjects (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${as.metadataUrl}"
          accept: application/json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /subject_identifier_types_supported
              hasValue: did:key
      - label: obtain an access token for the storage
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${as.tokenEndpoint}"
          bodyForm:
            grant_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange
            resource: "${as.realm}"
            subject_token: "${credential.didkey}"
            subject_token_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /access_token
              jsonType: string
              capture: accessToken
      - label: present it to the storage
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${test.container}"
          accept: application/lws+json
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Authorization
              headerValue: "Bearer ${accessToken}"
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 403, 404]
